     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin has no recognized therapeutic use. It's about 5 times the maximum labeled dose, and the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high no matter how well the kidneys and liver work. I can't enter it without a verification step beyond my own.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If the dose was a mistake**, give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) is the maximum standard dose.\n- **If there's a reason I don't know about**, such as a research protocol or an unusual formulation, please discuss it with your attending and inpatient pharmacy. If they approve, the order can go through whatever override or manual pathway your hospital uses for out-of-range doses.\n- **If the patient may already have taken a large amount of metformin**, that's an overdose, not an order. Contact poison control and the team right away.\n\nI can enter a corrected dose as soon as you have one."
      }
     ],
